      "text": [
        " رَجُلٍ قَضَى مُتْعَتَهُ ثُمَّ عَرَضَتْ لَهُ حَاجَةٌ أَرَادَ أَنْ يَخْرُجَ إِلَيْهَا قَالَ فَقَالَ فَلْيَغْتَسِلْ لِلْإِحْرَامِ وَ لْيُهِلَّ بِالْحَجِّ وَ لْيَمْضِ فِي حَاجَتِهِ وَ إِنْ لَمْ يَقْدِرْ عَلَى الرُّجُوعِ إِلَى مَكَّةَ مَضَى إِلَى عَرَفَاتٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hafs Bin Al Bakhtary, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding a man who fulfilled his <span class=\"iTxt\">Tumatto</span>, then a need presented itself to him, so he intended to go out to it’. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘So let him what for the <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span>, and let him begin with the Hajj, and let him go regarding his need; and if he is not able upon the return to Makkah, he should go to Arafaat’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ibn abu ‘Umayr has narrated from Hafs ibn al-Bakhtariy who has said the following: “About a man who completes Mut‘ah then because of a certain work wants to go out, he (the Imam) said, ‘He must take Ghusl (bath) for Ihram and say Talbiyah for al-Hajj, then go for his work and if he cannot return to Makkah he must go straight to ‘Arafat.’” "
        ]
      }
